Extension prompt-function:


| variable               | default value | description                                                  |
|------------------------+---------------+--------------------------------------------------------------|
|                        |               |                                                              |
| BOCL:*PROMPT-FUNCTION* | nil           | NIL, or a function designator.                               |
|                        |               | Signature; (lambda (stream) (format stream prompt-string))   |
|                        |               | The function is called to produce a new prompt for the REPL. |
|                        |               |                                                              |

When BOCL:*PROMPT-FUNCTION* is NIL, an implementation defined prompt
is used (eg. "~%bocl> ").

When BOCL:*PROMPT-FUNCTION* is set to a function designator, this
function is called to produce the prompt string used by the REPL for
each expression to read.

Example:
#+begin_src lisp
  (defun make-prompt-function ()
    (let ((histo-count 0))
      (lambda (stream)
        (format stream "~%~A #~A > "
                (package-name *package*)
                (incf histo-count)))))

  (setf bocl:*prompt-function* (make-prompt-function))
#+end_src

#+begin_src lisp
cl-user> (setf *prompt-function* (make-prompt-function))
#<ccl:compiled-lexical-closure (:internal make-prompt-function) #x30200247F21F>
cl-user> (loop repeat 3 collect (funcall *prompt-function* nil))
("
COMMON-LISP-USER #1 > " "
COMMON-LISP-USER #2 > " "
COMMON-LISP-USER #3 > ")
#+end_src
